    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49063" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράττης:</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ λίθος, ὑπὸ Θρακῶν</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θρακίας</span>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράττον:</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπερον, κόλουρον</span>, Id. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράττω</span></b> , 
			Att.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράσσω</span>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θραῦλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>frangible, brittle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			):—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θραῦρος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
